---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Pricing & insurance · DuBose, M.D." active="pricing" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Pricing</h1>
      <p class="lede">What $100 covers, what it doesn&rsquo;t, and how your insurance fits.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · The price card + access rate -->
  <section class="section band-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split even" style="align-items:start">
        <div class="price-card">
          <div class="amt">$100 <span>per month</span></div>
          <div class="per">per adult patient &middot; no per-visit charges</div>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Visits as your care needs them: video, home when needed,
            clinic space when that&rsquo;s better</li>
            <li>Direct messaging, answered in 1&ndash;2 business days</li>
            <li>Every result reviewed and explained</li>
            <li>Prescriptions managed; refills handled promptly</li>
            <li>Referrals and coordination with your other doctors</li>
            <li>Forms and paperwork included: disability, FMLA, letters,
            prior authorizations</li>
            <li>An unhurried annual review of everything</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:20px;color:var(--soft)">
            No enrollment fee. No contract. Cancel anytime, effective at
            the end of your billing month. Pay monthly by card or bank
            account.
          </p>
          <a class="btn" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
          <p class="small" style="margin-top:16px"><a class="quiet" style="font-size:14.5px" href="/agreement">Read the membership agreement &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="small soft">
            Each adult enrolls individually. A couple is $200. I care for
            adults only.
          </p>
          <h3 style="margin-top:32px">If $100 a month is a real barrier</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:10px">
            I keep a limited number of reduced-rate memberships for
            people who could not otherwise afford care. There is no
            application form. It is a conversation, with simple written
            criteria so it is fair. If cost is the thing stopping you,
            say so when we talk.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · What the fee does not cover -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>What the fee does not cover</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            My fee covers my work as your doctor. Care from others is
            billed by them, usually through your insurance.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Labs</b>
          <p>Through your insurance. Where I can get discounted direct
          pricing, I pass it to you at my cost and tell you the number
          before anything is drawn.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Imaging</b>
          <p>Through your insurance. I order what is needed and explain
          the results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicines</b>
          <p>Your pharmacy and insurance, as now. I help you find fair
          prices. Texas law does not allow doctors to sell medicines.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Specialists</b>
          <p>Through your insurance. I refer carefully and stay
          involved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Urgent care, ER, hospital</b>
          <p>Through your insurance, as today. My fee never replaces
          coverage for these.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
          This is why I recommend every member keep health coverage. The
          membership works alongside insurance, not instead of it.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · How your coverage fits -->
  <section class="section band-warm" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>How your coverage fits</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Whatever insurance you have, or none, you can join. The price
            and the care are the same for everyone.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Private insurance or none</b>
          <p>Sign up. That is all.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicare</b>
          <p>One extra document, a Medicare private contract, is required
          by federal rules. Your Medicare keeps paying for labs, imaging,
          specialists, prescriptions, and hospital care as before. My fee
          covers only my services.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicare Advantage</b>
          <p>Same private contract. If your plan is an HMO, we talk first
          about how your plan handles tests I order.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Texas Medicaid</b>
          <p>A short private-pay form is required by state rules. Your
          Medicaid keeps working outside our relationship. If you have
          traditional Medicaid, we talk first about how orders are
          covered.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
        <p>
          One exception: federal rules do not allow private arrangements
          with patients in certain combined Medicare and Medicaid
          programs (QMB and similar). If that is your situation, I will
          help you find good care instead.
        </p>
        <p>
          HSA funds: recent federal law may allow them for memberships
          like this one. Confirm with your tax advisor.
        </p>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · Why $100, and the limits -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>Why $100, and what&rsquo;s the catch</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Concierge practices typically charge $2,400 to $5,000 a year
            and still bill your insurance. I can charge $100 because the
            practice is small: no office building, no billing department,
            no staff, and a limited number of patients I know.
          </p>
          <p>
            The limits are stated, not hidden. I keep business hours. I
            am not an emergency service. I take real time away each year.
            And when my panel is full, it is full.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a class="quiet" href="/agreement">Read the full membership agreement &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Questions about your situation?</h2>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
